    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:EGu">EGu</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="130" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.5-2"/> gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.6-2"/> gehadod man gestalie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.7-2"/> oððe gefehte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.8-2"/> oððe forswerige oððe forlicge, gebete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> be þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.9-2"/> [þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.10-2"/>] seo dæde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.11"/> sy, swa be were swa be wite swa be lahslitte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.12"/>, ⁊ for Gode huru bete, swa canon tǽce, ⁊ þæs borh finde oððe carcern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.13"/> gebuge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="130" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf gehadod man gestalige oððe gefehte oððe forswerige oððe forlicge, gebete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> be ðam seo dǽd sy, swa be were swa be wite swa be lahslite, ⁊ for Gode huru bete, swa canon tæce, ⁊ þæs borh finde oððe carcer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.1"/> gebuge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.5"/><pb n="131" ed="#liebermann"/>Et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.6"/> si quis ordinatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.7"/> furetur uel prelietur uel periuret uel fornicetur, emendet, sicut factum erit, sic wera<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.8"/> sic wita sic lahslite, et erga Deum saltem emendet iuxta sanctorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.9"/> canonum doctrinam, et plegium faciat inde uel mittatur in carcere.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#EGu_3.lnote.oe.10"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="102" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ gyf gehadod man gestalie oððe gefehte oððe forswerige oððe forlicge, gebete þæt be þam þe seo dæd<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#EGu_3.attnote.fn.15"/> sy, swa be were swa be wite swa be lahslitte<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#EGu_3.attnote.fn.14"/>, ⁊ for Gode<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#EGu_3.attnote.fn.16"/> huru bete, swa canon tǽce, ⁊ þæs borh finde oððe carcern<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#EGu_3.attnote.fn.17"/> gebuge.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="4" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf gehadod man gestalie oððe gefeohte oððe forswerige oððe forlicge, gebete þæt be þam þe seo dæde sy swa be were swa be wite swa be lahslitte; and for Gode huru bete swa canon tæce and þæs borh finde oððe carcern gebuge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="131" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn ein geweihter Mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#EGu_3.lnote.de.1"/> stiehlt oder ficht oder falsch schwört<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#EGu_3.lnote.de.2"/> oder hurt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#EGu_3.lnote.de.3"/>, büsse er das, [je] nachdem dass die That sei, entweder durch [sein] Wergeld oder durch Strafgeld, beziehungsweise durch Rechtsbruchbusse, und büsse zumal vor Gott, wie der Kanon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#EGu_3.lnote.de.4"/> vorschreibt, und liefere für jenes [Strafgeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#EGu_3.lnote.de.5"/>] Bürgschaft oder wandere in den Kerker.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#EGu_3.lnote.de.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if an ordained man steals or fights or swears falsely or fornicates, let him pay for it according to what the deed is, either by [his] wergeld or by a fine, or by the penalty for breach of law, and above all let him do penance before God, as the canon prescribes, and let him find surety for that [fine] or go to prison.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="103" ed="#attenborough"/>And if a man in orders steals or fights, or commits perjury or adultery, he shall pay either wergeld or fine or <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>, according to the nature of the offence; and in any case shall he make compensation to God as the canon directs; and he shall find surety for the compensation or go to prison.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="5" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if a man in orders steals or fights or commits perjury or adultery, he shall atone according to the nature of the deed, either with his wergild or with a penalty or with lahslit; and indeed, he must do penance before God as the canon decrees and either find a surety or submit to imprisonment.</ab>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þam þe seo: þam seo B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De correctionibus ordinatorum <hi rend="italic">überschreibt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De correctionibus ordinatorum as heading in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Lond.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">fügt zu MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">MHkBr add uel</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weram sic witam <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weram sic witam TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ca. sa. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ca. sa. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rem <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rem Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> gefeohte <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> gefeohte <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to gefeohte H; gefeohte Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. H; fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above H; omitted in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dæd <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dæd Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-slite ⁊ for God <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-slite ⁊ for God Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert aus</hi> carcen <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> <hi rend="spaced">on</hi> carcern<hi rend="spaced">e</hi> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered from carcen H; <hi rend="italic">on</hi> carcern<hi rend="italic">e</hi> Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Geistliche 20a—c. g. 29b. g—i; Wergeld 30r. s</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Geistliche 20a—c. g. 29b. g—i; Wergeld 30r. s</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Meineid 15. a. Ausser Landes treibt Huren und meineidige Laien EGu 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Meineid 15. a. EGu 11 drives harlots and perjured laymen out of the country</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zölibat (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1ff.) ist hier noch nicht gefordert, wie schon seit Eadmund</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Celibacy (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1ff.) is not yet required here, as it already is from Eadmund on</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kanones 10a. Auch Egberti <hi rend="italic">Poenit.</hi> II 24 könnte gemeint sein. Im Volksgericht war also der Vertreter des bischöflichen Gerichts, das ja die Hälfte des Strafgelds empfing, anwesend</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kanones 10a. Egberti <hi rend="italic">Poenit.</hi> II 24 could also be meant. The representative of the bishop’s court, which after all received half of the fine, was therefore present in the popular court</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bürgschaft (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 14b. 17) wird auch für geistliche Zuchtbusse gestellt; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Northu 2; Stubbs <hi rend="italic">Constit. hist.</hi> I 244</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Surety (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 14b. 17) is also given for ecclesiastical disciplinary compensation; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Northu 2; Stubbs <hi rend="italic">Constit. hist.</hi> I 244</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_3.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gefängnis 8. b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gefängnis 8. b</seg></note>
